.SH DESCRIPTION
arcv\-test is wrapper for the  'shotplan' test tool which is used to run tests according to a plan file located in ${ARCV_TEST_DIR}/shotplan.yml
.PP
Actually, it calls another wrapper 'test_arcv' before shotplan is actually invoked.
.PP
All arguments passed on to this script are eventually forwarded to shotplan via test_arcv.
.PP
When testing a release, the symlink \fI\,/usr/bin/shotplan\/\fP to the source folder of shotplan must exist (there's no installable package yet for shotplan). Example:  sudo ln \fB\-s\fR \fI\,$HOME/riffian/Data/Data/admin/linux/shotplan\/\fP /usr/bin/shotplan
.PP
This script shall not be used when running tests in the docker container instead test_arcv shalll be called directly without reporting (\fB\-T\fR).
.PP
arcv\-test is the top\-level wrapper for the following purposes:
\- It provides usually API for a shell api app
\- arcv\-test handles the ARCV_DIR and ARCV_TEST_DIR variables depending whether ARCV_DIR is set to or not, determines whether a release is tested or a dev version, setting the variable properly when no.
\- In case of release testing, it runs install_arcv\-test.sh to install all necessary packages
\- provides the default options for running shotplan: \fB\-\-force\-defaults\fR \fB\-C\fR all \fB\-y\fR \fB\-i\fR
\- iIt opens a separate terminal at the left of the desktop in which will be run test_arcv
.PP
test_arcv is a low\-level wrapper script for the sake of :
\- Depending on the value of ARCV_TEST_DIR, setting ARCV_DIR accordingly
\- Running shotplan with the suitable plan file path.
\- Enabling to run shotplan with free arguments for other purposes, like extracting data from the plan by passing suitable arguments.
\- Running the tests inside docker
\- It redirects in a file "test\-report\-arcv\-<arcv version>\-<arcv revision>\-<date time>" the output of the test running, which can be viewed using cat <file>|more
.SH EXAMPLES
Testing with reporting (screenshots)
.IP
\f(CW$ arcv-test --report\fR
.PP
Testing without reporting
.IP
\f(CW$ arcv-test --T\fR
.PP
Testing starting from a certain plan, use option \-\-from, e.g
.IP
\f(CW$ arcv-test --from-init\fR
.PP
To run dev versions, set ARCV_DIR to the source folder, e.g.
.IP
# Put your test case description here
.IP
\f(CW$ export ARCV_DIR="\e$HOME/riffian/Data/Data/admin/linux/arcv"\fR
.PP
To test release version inside a docker
.IP
# ON HOST: this starts container and release package are auto installed
.IP
\f(CW$ arcv-test --C\fR
.IP
# INSIDE CONTAINER execute actual shot plan in interactive mode
.IP
\f(CW$ test_arcv --force-defaults -C all -y -T -i\fR
.IP
# INSIDE CONTAINER execute actual shot plan in automatic mode
.IP
\f(CW$ test_arcv --force-defaults -C all -y -T -a\fR
